course: dictionary
lesson: 8425
title: Ruth, an old word with a hidden meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Ruth is an old-fashioned word for pity or sorrow for others. It means feeling sad for someone who is suffering, and wanting to help them. You will hardly ever see ruth on its own today, but you will meet it hiding inside another word.
explain: Ruthless means without ruth, so without pity at all. A ruthless villain in a story does not care who gets hurt. Ruthlessly is the same idea in action: the thief acted ruthlessly. When you meet a new word, look for a smaller word inside it, like the ruth in ruthless.
explain: Ruth with a capital letter is a name. It is a girl's or woman's name, and the Bible has a book named after a woman called Ruth. Check the capital letter: a small ruth is the old word for pity, and a capital Ruth is a person.
fact: Ruth is a noun, and it is old-fashioned. It means pity or sorrow for others.
fact: Ruth is found today mostly in «ruthless», meaning without pity, and «ruthlessly», meaning in a pitiless way.
fact: Ruth is uncountable, so you do not say "a ruth" or "ruths".
fact: Ruth with a capital letter is a name. The Bible has a book named after a woman called Ruth.
fact: In the story, «Ruth promised Naomi, "Where you go I will go"», and she stayed with her mother-in-law.
exercise: In the word ruthless, the part ruth means: | Anger at the weather | A loud noise | *Pity or sorrow for others | A long journey
exercise: «Ruth was not an Israelite, yet she was welcomed and became the great-grandmother of King David.» Which word tells you Ruth was made to feel at home? | *welcomed | King | great-grandmother | Israelite
exercise: «In Israel Ruth gleaned, gathering the leftover grain in the field of Boaz.» What did Ruth gather? | Flowers | Wood for a fire | Gold coins | *Leftover grain
test: The word ruthless means: | Full of pity | Happy and kind | Very tired | *Without pity, cruel
test: «Ruth was a young widow from Moab, a foreign land, who would not leave her mother-in-law Naomi.» What does foreign mean? | Very old | Full of pity | Easy to find | *From another country
exam: Which is true of the old-fashioned noun ruth? | It is a type of animal | It only means a girl's name | It has a plural: ruths | *It means pity or sorrow for others
